WEBVTT

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:06.610
These are?

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.480
Shovels made with aluminum alloy!

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.490
You've already progressed to the 
point of manufacturing aluminum?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.450
I thought they'd help 
everyone in Elm Village.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.030
Yeah.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:26.570
Light, sturdy shovels will make farm work 
much easier than it ever was before.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.440
I'm sure they'll be delighted.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.640
It's only possible

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.170
because Masato-san got me lots 
of the resources I requested.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.180
Yeah.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.890
No one compares to him 
when it comes to earning money.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.710
Yeah, he's a really big help.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.230
I-I'm sorry, we were in the middle of talking.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.150
It's nothing to worry about.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.740
You should probably get some rest.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:01:00.460
B-But didn't you need me 
for something, Tsukasa-san?

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.950
I just wanted to check up on you.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.920
I was worried you might be 
pushing yourself too hard.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.780
I-In that case,

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.280
I'll get some rest.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.880
<i>Ringo-kun's not the only one.</i>

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.290
<i>Everyone is growing fatigued from 
this lifestyle we're not used to.</i>

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.610
Snow?

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.650
The Merchant will need recognition for 
the commotion he's probably causing

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.580
in Dormundt right about now.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.120
Working with water is 
rough this time of year.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.300
Cold!

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.030
It's snowing, too!

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.250
Oh, just don't go catching a cold.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.020
Hmm...

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.400
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.610
We won't let them mess with us anymore!

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:29.730
<b>It Seems Roo Can
\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDecide Her Own Worth!</b>

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.150
Don't worry about the profit margin!

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.500
Just buy up all the merchandise!

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.480
Yes, sir!

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:40.140
We can crush that puny trading company 
any time we want, with all our capital.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.480
They'll regret going up against Neutscheland.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.450
B-Bad news!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.980
What is it?!

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.460
Our trading company...

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:53.100
isn't getting a single product!

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.960
Wh-What?!

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.460
What...

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.400
What on earth...

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.660
Y-You people are...!

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:08.680
That's right.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.560
They're the traveling merchants you laid off.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.750
After you monopolized trade at the port,

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:18.570
you fired the merchants working the 
land routes in order to cut labor costs.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.320
By forcing the villagers to 
bring their goods in to you,

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.990
you made them bear the costs of the tariffs.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:27.710
Good grief, that's exactly 
the kind of cost-cutting

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.320
some idiot who only sees the 
numbers in his ledger would do.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:34.080
Since you let them go to waste, 
we've organized them all under our own company.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.950
Y-You don't mean...

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:39.450
Yeah. Our Elm Trading Company has signed

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.880
a three-year exclusive contract 
with these traveling merchants.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.720
Do you understand what that means?

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:48.720
All of their wares were purchased 
by the Elm Trading Company

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.720
before they ever set foot in this town.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.710
You can wait here with that 
stupid look on your face,

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.730
but you're never getting any merchandise.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.730
H-He's deceiving you all!

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:05.980
Our company will buy your wares for 
far more than his trashy company can!

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:07.550
It's not too late!

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.600
You can change your minds!

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.730
Elm Trading Company already told us 
that you'd pay more for our goods.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.590
We sold them knowing that already.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.340
Impossible! Why?!

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.020
It's obvious.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.380
Because we didn't want to sell to you.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.460
Wha?!

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.360
We risk our lives hauling these goods.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:35.520
We refuse to risk our lives for someone 
who'd fire us over his crappy accounting.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.920
You might say you'll buy our wares for 
more, but that's only for now, isn't it?

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:43.000
Once your war with Elm is over,
you'll go back to buying them on the cheap.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.420
Y-You have the wrong idea!

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.870
I won't lower prices anymore!

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:51.480
I deeply regret my past actions! So...

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.790
We don't trust you anymore.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.480
Jaccoi.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:06.260
What's most important to a 
business isn't money. It's trust.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.870
So long as you have trust, 
you can earn money again.

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:14.080
I can't believe threw away
the trust you'd established

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.640
with the merchants and the villages,
just for a little extra money.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:20.990
There's no future for a business 
that's lost its trust.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.650
You went too far.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:28.250
He really did crush Neutscheland in a week...

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.970
However, it would also be going too far 
to crush you and Neutscheland right here.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:33.780
Huh?

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.640
Be it Elm or Neutscheland,

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:40.890
it's just not healthy for any one 
business to monopolize the market.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.720
So why don't those of us here talk it out?

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:48.090
Let's discuss the future 
of trade and the economy

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.620
here in Dormundt and the 
territory of Findolf.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:58.310
Though we plan on taking advantage
of you, so you'd better be prepared.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.980
Y-Yes...

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:13.960
Which one, hm...

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.870
Hey, why didn't you crush Neutscheland?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:16.860
Hm?

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:20.620
Because there were more 
drawbacks in crushing them than not.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.120
Drawbacks?

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:26.490
We couldn't keep so many 
traveling merchants employed.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:30.910
I always intended to throw them all back 
at Neutscheland, once I broke Jaccoi's spirit.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.650
Th-Then the contracts with those merchants...

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:37.010
Yeah, they were empty contracts.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:41.600
You're telling me this after 
all that talk about trust?

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.900
Are you actually a bad person?

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.840
Of course I am.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:51.650
In the world I'm from, I'm a 
merchant known as the Demon Lord.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:54.280
Demon Lord!

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.780
We found you, you stupid brat!

00:07:57.130 --> 00:08:01.290
You two! What do you think you're doing, 
walking around with someone else's goods?!

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:02.980
Goods?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.690
That brat is a slave, and she's ours to sell!

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.130
Now hurry up and give her back!

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.310
Hey!

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:15.470
Huh? You got a problem here?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.400
Rooko.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.190
Shall I save you?

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:26.950
Save...

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.070
One day...

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:42.620
I'm going to become a good merchant.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.240
Then I'll earn lots of money,

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.460
and use it...

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.750
to buy back my mother and father.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:56.440
But all the money I have left 
over afterward, I'll give to you.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:57.790
I promise!

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:00.010
I won't let you take a loss on this!

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.020
So, Teacher...

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.520
Please buy me right here and now!

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.180
What are you going on about? You brat!

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.110
Well said, Rooko.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.040
I'd like to buy this slave,

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.530
at 100 times the market price.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.370
Oh!

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.370
You've got no complaints, do you?

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.290
Y-You're not getting a refund!

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.880
Yeah. So we have a contract.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:33.380
The courage and willpower you displayed

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:37.050
is a thousand times more valuable
than the money I just spent.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:42.300
Teacher!

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.940
Now let's make them regret this.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.950
We'll show them they were 
huge fools for passing up

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:49.610
this huge fortune for a paltry sum.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.970
Sorry, Elch,

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:55.920
for using up all the money we earned.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.290
It's fine.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:01.120
You already earned us so much that 
no one will mind what you spent.

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:04.660
I never knew that it could feel this good

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:08.460
to spend money on something.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:11.820
I know, right?

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.550
This is why I can never stop earning money!

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.710
So it all ended being a huge victory 
for Elm Trading Company!

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:23.720
That's the Demon Lord of the 
Financial World for you.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.350
There's a reason the Merchant 
is known as an economic emperor.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:30.100
I'm glad to see you're enjoying yourself, too.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.810
A city full of information is precisely 
where a journalist belongs.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:40.080
So, about those inquiries you requested.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.950
First, the magic.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.860
In this world, there are four 
different types of spirits:

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.990
Fire, Water, Wind, and Earth.

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:51.320
Communicating with them 
allows miracles to occur.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.940
And, well, their powers are about 
what you would imagine them to be.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:57.480
But people who can actually
use magic are scarce.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.130
Here in the territory of Findolf,

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:03.350
the only one who can is the mage 
officer living in the lord's castle.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.430
Hmm...

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:08.800
What about magic capable of crossing worlds 
or summoning someone from another world?

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.830
<i>I don't know yet.</i>

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.850
<i>Though since magic itself 
is so rare to begin with,</i>

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:15.860
<i>there isn't much information on that.</i>

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.080
I see.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:20.360
Well, we're doing well just gaining an 
understanding of their concept of magic.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:21.760
Thank you.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:24.140
<i>Nin, nin! You're welcome.</i>

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:24.870
<i>So...</i>

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:26.520
One more thing.

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:29.530
It looks like we're out of 
luck on the seven heroes.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:30.520
<i>What?</i>

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:31.800
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:35.560
Well, there is a religion 
known as the Seven-Light Faith

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:38.460
that might be related to them, at least.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.120
<i>The Seven-Light Faith, huh?</i>

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:41.900
Yeah.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:44.160
But that Seven-Light Faith

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:49.350
was destroyed several centuries 
ago by the Freyjagard Empire.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.560
It wasn't just the Seven-Light Faith, either.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.230
All of the religions that used 
to exist on this continent

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:59.690
were destroyed, root and branch.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:04.680
Freyjagard policy 
of "survival of the fittest"

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:09.120
didn't allow any gods to 
be placed above the empire.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.620
Religious oppression, huh?

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:15.450
<i>I carefully checked the villages 
surrounding Dormundt to be sure,</i>

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:19.320
<i>but they didn't have any religions, 
or even have records of any.</i>

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:20.510
I see.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:24.520
However, that's still our only clue 
as to how to return to our world.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:28.460
We'll have to search for it, even if it means 
turning over every stone on the continent.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:29.610
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:33.020
<i>There's a problem, though.</i>

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:37.160
People need a travel permit 
from Marquis Findolf

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:40.820
in order to leave the territory 
we're in right now.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:46.070
This Marquis Findolf is also 
one hell of a shitty bastard.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:48.140
A shitty bastard?

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:49.750
Tsukasa-dono!

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.270
It's done!

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.600
It's finished, bear!

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.390
Hm? Done? What's done?

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:58.520
I worked beary hard with 
Aoi-chan to make it!

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:59.290
Oh, I finally did something 
befitting a politician

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:00.970
It bears seeing at once!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.460
and had some public facilities created.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.900
Public facilities?

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.180
What a nice bath!

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.940
You made a public bathhouse 
for the villagers?

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.270
I'm impressed.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.960
How is it, how is it?

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:24.650
If I wear this, I can bathe 
alongside everyone, right, Tsukasa?

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.230
That's right.

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:31.050
Ringo-kun, you don't have to 
force yourself to join us, you know.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:34.160
I... I'll be fine.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.400
Oh, Lyrule, where were you?

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.210
I went to get this.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:42.420
Tsukasa looked like he injured his hand.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.660
Yeah...

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.920
I was doing work I'm not used to.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:50.420
What's this?

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:53.030
A salve made from horse oil.

00:13:55.510 --> 00:14:00.830
Applying this to the wound will ease 
the pain and help it heal faster.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:01.770
I see.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:04.650
Thank you, Lyrule.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.410
B-Bad news!

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.390
Some of the villagers that went hunting

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:13.370
ran into a monster called 
 the Chief of the Forest!

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:14.970
Huh?

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:25.690
There's a large heat signature 
500 meters ahead.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:35.370
Masato...

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.220
Oh, has everyone come out to greet me?

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:40.520
No, something's off.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:43.080
Something must have happened.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.830
A-Aoi?!

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:04.780
You don't need to worry about her.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.840
How is everyone else?

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:10.860
M-Mayor Ulga...

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.230
Huh?

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:32.820
So you're the Chief of the Forest?

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:40.300
H-He stopped breathing a moment ago.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:41.410
I see.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:44.570
If he's only just stopped breathing, 
he should be fine.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:46.960
Isn't that right, Keine-kun?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.220
Yes, of course.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:06.680
Left fifth through tenth rib, all broken.

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:09.070
Abdominal lacerations, colon rupture...

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.140
Everything below the diaphragm is poking out.

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:14.030
He's passed out from hemorrhagic shock,

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:18.540
and he's been in cardiac arrest for 
just under three minutes, I believe.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:21.320
Okay, okay.

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:23.540
This should be no problem.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.170
Beginning operation.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.680
I-Incredible...

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:25.690
She's sealing up the wound.

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:28.070
Damaged organs repaired.

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:31.190
Surgical treatment completed.

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:33.640
Liquid oxygen injected.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:35.950
Now commencing cardiopulmonary resuscitation.

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:58.760
All treatment completed.

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:04.250
He should wake up in two to three days.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.480
Father...

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:13.110
Good work.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:14.360
My...

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:20.410
This hardly even counts as work.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.350
Right, Aoi-san?

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:24.990
Indeed. That was a piece of cake.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:29.780
Well, let's head back to Elm Village.

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:34.120
Aoi and Keine are with them. 
They'll make it back safely.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:40.470
That's...

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:46.070
Peasants, bow your heads!

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:50.150
Before you stands the Captain of 
Marquis Findolf's Guardian Knights,

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:54.650
the Silver Knight, Inzagi!

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:57.560
Guardian Knights?!

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:02.340
Hmph, this village reeks of beast.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.030
Seize them.

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:06.840
Hm?

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:14.130
You are suspected of treason against the state.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.280
Wh-What do you mean?!

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:21.020
You have used illegal means to gather 
gold coins within these lands.

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:22.090
Illegal?

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:25.140
We earned that money doing proper business.

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:29.370
If you need proof, I'll show you 
our ledger and our business permit!

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:30.960
There's no need.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:35.020
It's a sin for vulgar peasants such 
as yourselves to even touch gold.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:39.740
Every gold coin is engraved with the 
dragon crest of the Freyjagard Empire.

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:43.850
Allowing your filthy hands 
to touch that dragon crest

00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:46.240
is akin to treason against the state!

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:51.770
Marquis Findolf, lord of these 
lands, is highly offended.

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:53.790
That's hardly even a pretext!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.770
Silence, peasants.

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:59.930
Our noble words are worth 
far more than your lives.

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:02.040
Should we tell you to live, 
then you shall live,

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:04.470
and if we say you die, you die.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.440
This is an order directly 
from the lord himself.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:11.230
"Burn all traitors who don't 
know their place at the stake."

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:12.510
Teacher!

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:13.300
Tsk.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:23.360
Wh-What is all this?

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:26.080
Winona! It's no use! We can't find them!

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:27.820
None of them are here!

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:30.760
Th-They could still be inside.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:32.090
We have to rescue them!

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:33.370
Let's go, everyone!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.170
Yeah!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:35.660
Do not!

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:38.920
Lunging into a burning building is suicide!

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:40.630
B-But...

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.250
Don't worry.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:47.450
We have someone capable
of escaping welded-shut coffins.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.600
Exactly!

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:55.850
Everyone, it's all right now!

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:01.450
Darling!

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:02.440
Father!

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:04.890
Elch, you're safe!

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:06.470
Y-Yeah...

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:09.410
Thanks to him.

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:13.720
You did well, Akatsuki.

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:16.090
We're lucky you were here.

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:18.540
Yeah, although...

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:21.760
We have trouble, Tsukasa.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:22.630
Hm?

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:26.380
The ones who attacked this village 
called themselves the Guardian Knights,

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.350
and they said they had direct 
orders from the lord.

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:31.100
The lord?

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:34.140
His name was Marquis Findolf, wasn't it?

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:46.240
Where is Lyrule?
